libdiginet (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fuzz: the transport coverage floor at the 422 lines its corpus reaches
    once the unreached paths are gone
  * fuzz/README.md: 188 records
  * fuzz: the latest sabotage names the line of its check
  * fuzz: an e0 ends an online session whatever a failed wake left of the
    handshake
  * 0.1.3: the changelog says what the release holds, the fuzz counts what
    the harnesses hold
  * fuzz: the keepalive sabotage names the line of its check
  * fuzz: the sabotage patches and records meet their checks on the
    Control|24 e1 model
  * transport: online on the a0 and an e1 naming this host, for every desk
  * fuzz: the records and contracts name the lines they break again
  * transport: a Control|24 announces e1 in session, and its e0 ends the
    session
  * fuzz: the retake-other-if wake record without a comment opener inside the
    comment
  * docs, fuzz: the moved-desk rule in protocol.md, the record counts in
    fuzz/README.md (#40)
  * fuzz: the records, contracts and sabotage headers name the lines they
    break again
  * mux: an e1 naming any MAC of this host is this host's session (#40)
  * 0.1.3: a Control|24's e0 answered with an e2 at send counter 0
  * fuzz: the e2 counter records on seeds that reach them,
    c24-e0-after-keepalive added
  * transport: every e2 carries send counter 0, on which alone a Control|24
    takes a session
  * fuzz: an e0 that ends a Control|24 session without an e1 shows in the
    state, not the e2 count
  * fuzz: the records and sabotage patches name the lines they break again
  * transport: answer_e0 in the config, the probe off; the fuzz model owes
    the e2 an e0 asks for
  * transport: a Control|24's e0 is answered with an e2, since it ACKs host
    frames out of session

